// ATTACHING A REMOTE IMAGE, AS A MODELED OPERATION RATHER THAN A SHELL SCRIPT. extdeps.bmc.megarac
// described this API in prose for months and carried no transport, so the first attach against a
// Mt. Collins unit was driven by hand-written curl — the unmodeled realization DESIGN §6 names, and
// the reason the netboot lane could not claim its image was procured through .dag. The service rows
// made the surface reachable; this module is the caller that makes it reached.
//
// EVERY STEP READS BACK, AND THAT IS FORCED BY THE CONTROLLER'S OWN BEHAVIOUR rather than chosen for
// rigour. gunbc.machine_intake_mtcollins1_diskless_boot_receipt records two measured cases of this
// firmware answering HTTP 500 WHILE THE WRITE TOOK EFFECT: PUT media/general (code 16425) with the
// share re-mounting anyway, and stop-media (code 1411) with the following attach succeeding. An
// operation that treated a non-zero exit as refusal would refuse a write that worked, and the caller
// would then retry or abort against a controller whose state had already moved. So success here is
// never an exit status; it is the configurations listing naming the image.
//
// THE IMAGE INDEX IS RESOLVED, NEVER ASSUMED. start-media takes an image_index, and the controller
// assigns indices by its own enumeration of the share — the same file was index 0 on one scan and
// index 1 after another image appeared. A baked index attaches whatever now occupies that slot,
// which on a share holding a memtest ISO and an installer ISO is a silent wrong-boot rather than a
// failure. The index is read from the images listing by matching the image NAME.
//
// THE IMAGES LISTING ENUMERATES WHAT IS AVAILABLE TO ATTACH, NOT WHAT THE SHARE HOLDS, and an
// earlier revision of this module got that exactly backwards in a way worth recording because the
// wrong diagnosis had a dangerous remedy attached to it. Measured on this unit 2026-09-06: with two
// ISOs in the export, /remote/images listed both; after start-media attached one, the listing
// returned ONLY THE OTHER, and the survivor's image_index moved from 1 to 0. The attached image had
// not vanished — it had moved to /remote/configurations, which is where a presented image lives.
//
// THE EARLIER READING WAS THAT THE LISTING IS A CACHE THAT GOES STALE, with the remedy "re-assert
// mount_cd". That remedy appeared to work, and the reason it appeared to work is the problem:
// toggling mount_cd DETACHES EVERYTHING, which is what returns the image to the available pool. A
// remedy that works by undoing the desired state is worse than no remedy, and it was written into
// an operator-facing message on a lane whose entire purpose is hosts booted from that medium.
//
// WHAT THE HAZARD IS, AT THE STRENGTH IT WAS ACTUALLY MEASURED, because an earlier revision of this
// paragraph overstated it in the same breath as retracting an overstatement. It claimed the toggle
// pulls the running root out from under a booted host. That is the MECHANISM — the presented medium
// is withdrawn, and casper reads the read-only lower layer from it on demand rather than from RAM,
// per this lane's own boot receipt — but it is not what was observed. The toggle WAS performed on
// this unit while it was booted from the medium, and the running installer survived it: measured
// afterwards over serial console, still interactive at its own menu. The controller is configured
// rmedia_retry_count 3 / rmedia_retry_interval 15, and the system was idle at a prompt rather than
// reading, either of which may explain the survival.
//
// SO THE HONEST STATEMENT IS THAT THE BLAST RADIUS IS UNQUANTIFIED, not that it is catastrophic and
// not that it is safe. One observation of one idle host is not evidence that a toggle during heavy
// reads is survivable, and the remedy is still wrong for the reason that does not depend on any of
// this: it "fixes" the listing by undoing the attachment the caller asked for.
//
// SO THE ORDER OF READS IS LOAD-BEARING AND CONFIGURATIONS COMES FIRST. Asking the available list
// whether an already-attached image is present is asking the wrong authority a question it answers
// "no" for the one reason that means SUCCESS. That is what made the operation non-idempotent: a
// second converge against a correctly-attached host refused, which for a converge step is the
// failure mode that matters most, since converge is run repeatedly by construction.
// THE CLEANUP OUTCOME IS CARRIED BESIDE THE ATTACH OUTCOME, never folded into it. Whether the
// image attached and whether the session was released are different facts with different owners: a
// successful attach that leaked a session is still a successful attach, and reporting it as a
// failure would hide the thing that worked while a caller retried it and leaked another. The
// controller's session table is finite — this lane exhausted one service's sessions by opening one
// per probe and closing none — so the release has to be observable rather than assumed.
//
// A LOST OR UNCLASSIFIED GET IS NOT A RELEASED SESSION. CloseSession's own exit is discarded on
// purpose (this firmware has answered HTTP 401 on DELETE while an independent probe showed the
// session gone). The standing is the probe that follows, on a route this firmware serves
// (ProbeSessionOnMediaRoute), with curl --fail-with-body plus a trailing `%{http_code}` write-out,
// so a timeout (`000`), a drop, and an HTTP 401 are different stdout. Only a 401/403 after a
// SUCCEEDING probe before the close, under a parsed X-CSRFTOKEN, is evidence the cookie no longer
// authenticates; every other outcome, and any probe that used a sentinel header, stays
// SessionReleaseRefused.
type SessionRelease
  = SessionReleased
  | SessionReleaseRefused { detail: String }
  | SessionReleaseNotAttempted

type MegaRacAttachResult {
  outcome: MegaRacAttachOutcome
  session_release: SessionRelease
  baseline: MegaRacMediaBaseline?
}

// THE ONE SUCCESS IS A READY PRESENTATION, AND IT CARRIES HOW IT WAS REACHED AND WHAT WAS SEEN.
// Already-presented, freshly attached and replaced-then-attached are three ROUTES to the same
// verdict, and all three pass the same readiness fold (side chat on gunbc#12425): a name match on
// an already-presented row is not readiness, and was the gap that let a boot power on over a
// presentation that had not started.
type MegaRacAttachOutcome
  = MegaRacPresentationReady { route: MegaRacAttachRoute, evidence: MegaRacPresentationEvidence }
  | MegaRacReadinessTimedOut { image_name: NonEmptyStr, route: MegaRacAttachRoute, last: ReadinessLook, deadline: EpochMs, looks: Int, cd_before_any_write: CdErrorReading, cd_at_refusal: CdErrorReading }
  | MegaRacMediaStateUnestablished { image_name: NonEmptyStr, route: MegaRacAttachRoute, look: ReadinessLook, looks: Int, cd_before_any_write: CdErrorReading, cd_at_ready: CdErrorReading, general_at_ready: MegaRacRawRead }
  | MegaRacMediaStateUnestablishedBeforeWrite { cd_before_any_write: CdErrorReading, reason: NonEmptyStr }
  | MegaRacReadinessRefused { image_name: NonEmptyStr, route: MegaRacAttachRoute, look: ReadinessLook, looks: Int, cd_before_any_write: CdErrorReading, cd_at_refusal: CdErrorReading }
  | MegaRacReadinessClockUnreadable { image_name: NonEmptyStr, route: MegaRacAttachRoute, detail: String }
  | MegaRacReadinessClockIncoherent { image_name: NonEmptyStr, route: MegaRacAttachRoute, opened_at: EpochMs, previous: EpochMs?, look: ReadinessLook, looks: Int }
  | MegaRacConfigurationsUnreadable { detail: String }
  | MegaRacShareMismatch { expected: MegaRacShareBinding, observed: MegaRacObservedShare }
  | MegaRacShareUnreadable { detail: String }
  | MegaRacPresentationObserved { share: ShareBindingStanding, readiness: AttachReadiness, cd_error: CdErrorReading, general: MegaRacRawRead, configurations: MegaRacRawRead }
  | MegaRacSessionRefused { detail: String }
  | MegaRacSessionTokenUnreadable { detail: String }
  | MegaRacImagesUnreadable { detail: String }
  | MegaRacImageListingEmpty
  | MegaRacImageListingUnparseable { detail: String }
  | MegaRacImageNotEnumerated { image_name: NonEmptyStr }
  | MegaRacImageOfferedAmbiguously { image_name: NonEmptyStr, image_indices: List<String> }
  | MegaRacForeignImagePresented { image_name: String, configurations: String }
  | MegaRacSeveralImagesPresented { configurations: String }
  | MegaRacStaleDetachNotAdmitted { stale_image: String, reason: NonEmptyStr }
  | MegaRacStaleDetachUnconfirmed { detach: MegaRacDetachEvidence, reason: NonEmptyStr }
  | MegaRacRedirectionUncatalogued { image_name: String, wire: Int, configurations: String }
  | MegaRacRefreshClockUnreadable { detail: String, detach: MegaRacDetachEvidence }
  | MegaRacListingUnparseableAfterDetach { detail: String, detach: MegaRacDetachEvidence }
  | MegaRacOfferedAmbiguouslyAfterDetach { image_name: NonEmptyStr, image_indices: List<String>, detach: MegaRacDetachEvidence }
  | MegaRacNotEnumeratedAfterRefresh { image_name: NonEmptyStr, detach: MegaRacDetachEvidence, standing: RemoteMediaMountStanding }

// THREE INDICES, THREE CONCEPTS, NEVER JOINED. image_list_index is the image's position in
// /remote/images at the look that resolved it (absent on the already-presented route, where no
// listing was consulted); media_index is the virtual device slot; session_index is the redirection
// session. See configuration_row_reading for the nicknaming failure that joining them was.
type MegaRacAttachRoute
  = RouteAlreadyPresented
  | RouteAttached { image_list_index: String, start: MegaRacWriteAnswer }
  | RouteReplaced { image_list_index: String, detach: MegaRacDetachEvidence, start: MegaRacWriteAnswer }

type MegaRacPresentationEvidence {
  firmware: BmcFirmwareReleaseIdentity
  image_name: NonEmptyStr
  media_index: String?
  session_index: String?
  redirection_wire: Int
  established_at: EpochMs
  looks: Int
  cd_before_any_write: CdErrorReading
  cd_at_ready: CdErrorReading
  general_at_ready: MegaRacRawRead
}

// THE STOP COMMAND'S ANSWER AND THE READ-BACK ARE TWO FACTS AND BOTH ARE KEPT. This firmware has
// answered 1411 "Error stopping the remote media redirection" to a stop after which configurations
// read image '' and status 0: the read-back establishes the detach, and the error is retained
// beside it rather than discarded. A success whose read-back still presents the image, or cannot be
// read, establishes nothing.
// WHAT A WRITE'S OWN ANSWER ESTABLISHES, and it is never the effect (side-chat review 5332343434).
// Four facts, not folded together:
//   not issued        -- no command ran; the reason says why;
//   accepted          -- curl exited 0 with the controller's body;
//   HTTP error answer -- curl exited 22 under --fail-with-body: the controller sent a COMPLETE error
//                        response, kept verbatim (this build has answered such bodies to writes that
//                        took effect);
//   effect uncertain  -- any other exit: a timeout (28), a transport failure, an abort -- with the
//                        exit code and every byte that did arrive kept, never read as a complete answer.
// The verdict is keyed on curl's TYPED exit code, the same fact
// gunbc.machine_intake_mtcollins1_boot_diagnostic_bundle bmc_curl_read_cause keys on (review 71971);
// stderr is kept as evidence, never parsed for the verdict. In every case the read-back decides the
// effect.
type MegaRacWriteAnswer
  = WriteNotIssued { reason: NonEmptyStr }
  | WriteAccepted { body: String }
  | WriteAnsweredHttpError { body: String, stderr: String }
  | WriteEffectUncertain { exit_code: Int, partial_body: String, stderr: String }

data curl_exit_http_error: Int = 22

fn megarac_write_answer(exit_code: Int, body: String, stderr: String) -> MegaRacWriteAnswer {
  if exit_code == 0 {
    WriteAccepted { body: body }
  } else if exit_code == curl_exit_http_error {
    WriteAnsweredHttpError { body: body, stderr: stderr }
  } else {
    WriteEffectUncertain { exit_code: exit_code, partial_body: body, stderr: stderr }
  }
}

type MegaRacDetachEvidence {
  stale_image: String
  media_index: String
  command: MegaRacWriteAnswer
  readback_read: Bool
  readback: String
  cd_after_stop: CdErrorReading
  general_after_stop: MegaRacRawRead
}

// WHICH PRESENTED IMAGES THIS ATTACH MAY REPLACE, AND WHETHER IT MAY WRITE ANYTHING DESTRUCTIVE
// NOW. Both are the caller's policy and neither is this operation's to decide: the replaceable set
// is named by a seeded-media STEM, so recognition is the inverse of the naming authority
// (extdeps.provisioning.ubuntu_seeded_install_media ubuntu_seeded_install_media_name_digest_prefix)
// rather than a prefix list authored here; and the admission is established by the caller from its
// own hold and its own power observation. The admission is consulted ONLY when a destructive step
// is needed, so a caller whose host is on still converges the already-attached case as a no-op.
//
// THE DESTRUCTIVE STEP IS stop-media: against a host running from the medium it withdraws what the
// host is reading from, which is why the admission names a host that is off and held.
type MegaRacDetachAdmission
  = MegaRacDetachAdmitted
  | MegaRacDetachNotAdmitted { reason: NonEmptyStr }

// ONE SESSION ROUTE, TWO TASKS. Converging writes; observing only reads, and exists because a
// presentation observed ready can be lost before or after the boot-device and power handoff that
// consumes it (side chat on gunbc#12425: a re-read narrows the window, it cannot close it, so the
// loss after the handoff has to be an observed outcome too). Both go through the same session
// open, token parse and observed release, so an observation cannot leak a session either.
type MegaRacSessionTask
  = MegaRacConverge { policy: MegaRacReplacementPolicy }
  | MegaRacObserve { share: MegaRacShareBinding }

type MegaRacReplacementPolicy {
  replaceable_seeded_stem: NonEmptyStr
  detach: MegaRacDetachAdmission
  share: MegaRacShareBinding
}

// THE SHARE AN IMAGE NAME IS RESOLVED IN, AS A TYPED BINDING. The controller presents an image by
// NAME from whatever share settings/media/general points it at, so every name check in this module
// is only as good as that pointer: a same-named file on another server or path would pass every one
// of them. The binding is the caller's fact (which server and export this unit boots from); the
// member spellings are the controller's (extdeps.bmc.megarac megarac_op_media_config). It is read
// before any write on every route, including the already-presented one, because a presentation of
// the right name from the wrong share is the wrong medium.
type MegaRacShareType
  = MegaRacShareNfs
  | MegaRacShareCifs

fn megarac_share_type_wire(t: MegaRacShareType) -> String {
  match t {
    MegaRacShareNfs => "nfs"
    MegaRacShareCifs => "cifs"
  }
}

type MegaRacShareBinding {
  server_address: NonEmptyStr
  source_path: NonEmptyStr
  share_type: MegaRacShareType
}

type MegaRacObservedShare {
  server_address: String
  source_path: String
  share_type: String
  mount_cd: String
  remote_media_support: String
}

type ShareBindingStanding
  = ShareBound
  | ShareMismatch { observed: MegaRacObservedShare }
  | ShareUnreadable { detail: String }

type MediaGeneralShareRead
  = MediaGeneralShareObserved { observed: MegaRacObservedShare }
  | MediaGeneralShareUnreadable { detail: String }

// THE CD ERROR CODE IS AN OBSERVED NUMBER, AND NO MEANING IS ESTABLISHED FOR ANY VALUE.
// settings/media/general carries cd_error_code beside mount_cd. Boot run 36721915217 (an executed
// receipt) read 16 before any write, after its own stop and at readiness, while the configurations row
// read Started with session_index 0. That is a COEXISTENCE: the value was already present before the
// attempt stopped anything, so it does not show what produced it. No public document or executed
// receipt gives any value a cause, so the model keeps the raw observation and names none. Two readings:
//   CdErrorNone    -- 0;
//   CdErrorNonzero -- any other value, with the firmware it was read from.
// An UNREAD code is never a reading, and withholds everywhere.
type MegaRacCdErrorCode
  = CdErrorNone
  | CdErrorNonzero { wire: Int, firmware: BmcFirmwareReleaseIdentity }

// POLICY, NOT A DECODED CAUSE. A nonzero code with nothing presented admits the attach only when it is
// 16 read from firmware 0.32: boot run 36721915217 read exactly that before it attached, and the
// attached presentation reached Started and the run proceeded. Admitting it claims that the run
// proceeded under this reading, not what the code means. Every other nonzero code, and 16 on another
// build, has no such run behind it, so the fresh-presentation experiment must be admitted first.
data cd_error_attach_policy_wire: Int = 16

fn cd_error_attach_policy_admits(code: MegaRacCdErrorCode) -> Bool {
  match code {
    CdErrorNone => true
    CdErrorNonzero { wire: w, firmware: f } => w == cd_error_attach_policy_wire && bmc_firmware_release_identity_eq(a: f, b: megarac_firmware_0_32)
  }
}

fn megarac_cd_error_code_of_wire(firmware: BmcFirmwareReleaseIdentity, wire: Int) -> MegaRacCdErrorCode {
  if wire == 0 { CdErrorNone }
  else { CdErrorNonzero { wire: wire, firmware: firmware } }
}

type CdErrorReading
  = CdErrorRead { code: MegaRacCdErrorCode }
  | CdErrorUnread { detail: String }

fn cd_error_reading(body: String, firmware: BmcFirmwareReleaseIdentity) -> CdErrorReading {
  match parse_json_document(s: body) {
    JsonDocumentUnreadable { gap: _ } => CdErrorUnread { detail: body }
    JsonDocumentParsed { value: v } =>
      match json_number_member(doc: v, key: "cd_error_code") {
        Absent => CdErrorUnread { detail: concat("cd_error_code missing: ", body) }
        Present { value: w } =>
          match parse_int(s: w) {
            Absent => CdErrorUnread { detail: concat("cd_error_code is not an integer: ", w) }
            Present { value: n } => CdErrorRead { code: megarac_cd_error_code_of_wire(firmware: firmware, wire: n) }
          }
      }
  }
}

// PURE, over the general-settings document. Every member is required: a document missing one is
// unreadable, never "matches by default". Empty server/path/type are valid observations (a factory
// or cleared share). share_binding_standing consumes this decode; it does not re-read the wire.
fn observe_media_general_share(body: String) -> MediaGeneralShareRead {
  match parse_json_document(s: body) {
    JsonDocumentUnreadable { gap: _ } => MediaGeneralShareUnreadable { detail: body }
    JsonDocumentParsed { value: v } =>
      match json_string_member(doc: v, key: "cd_remote_server_address") {
        Absent => MediaGeneralShareUnreadable { detail: concat("cd_remote_server_address missing: ", body) }
        Present { value: server } =>
          match json_string_member(doc: v, key: "cd_remote_source_path") {
            Absent => MediaGeneralShareUnreadable { detail: concat("cd_remote_source_path missing: ", body) }
            Present { value: path } =>
              match json_string_member(doc: v, key: "cd_remote_share_type") {
                Absent => MediaGeneralShareUnreadable { detail: concat("cd_remote_share_type missing: ", body) }
                Present { value: kind } =>
                  match json_number_member(doc: v, key: "mount_cd") {
                    Absent => MediaGeneralShareUnreadable { detail: concat("mount_cd missing: ", body) }
                    Present { value: mount } =>
                      match json_number_member(doc: v, key: "remote_media_support") {
                        Absent => MediaGeneralShareUnreadable { detail: concat("remote_media_support missing: ", body) }
                        Present { value: remote } =>
                          MediaGeneralShareObserved {
                            observed: MegaRacObservedShare {
                              server_address: server,
                              source_path: path,
                              share_type: kind,
                              mount_cd: mount,
                              remote_media_support: remote,
                            },
                          }
                      }
                  }
              }
          }
      }
  }
}

// mount_cd must be 1 because a share that is configured but not mounted offers nothing to attach.
fn share_binding_standing(body: String, expected: MegaRacShareBinding) -> ShareBindingStanding {
  match observe_media_general_share(body: body) {
    MediaGeneralShareUnreadable { detail: d } => ShareUnreadable { detail: d }
    MediaGeneralShareObserved { observed: o } =>
      if o.server_address != (expected.server_address as String)
        || o.source_path != (expected.source_path as String)
        || o.share_type != megarac_share_type_wire(t: expected.share_type)
        || o.mount_cd != "1" {
        ShareMismatch { observed: o }
      } else {
        ShareBound
      }
  }
}

// THE CSRF TOKEN IS READ FROM THE PARSED DOCUMENT, not scraped. The shell version matched a regex
// over the response body, which is a second reading of JSON beside the one this repository already
// owns; extdeps.languages.json.parse is the single recognition authority and a document it cannot
// parse is unreadable rather than partially believed.
fn json_string_member(doc: JsonValue, key: String) -> String? {
  match json_object_unique_member(v: doc, key: key) {
    JsonMemberFound { value: v } =>
      match v {
        JsonString { value: s } => Present { value: s }
        JsonNull => none
        JsonBool { value: _ } => none
        JsonNumber { lexeme: _ } => none
        JsonArray { elements: _ } => none
        JsonObject { members: _ } => none
      }
    JsonMemberAbsent => none
    JsonMemberDuplicated { count: _ } => none
    JsonMemberNotAnObject => none
  }
}

fn json_number_member(doc: JsonValue, key: String) -> String? {
  match json_object_unique_member(v: doc, key: key) {
    JsonMemberFound { value: v } =>
      match v {
        JsonNumber { lexeme: n } => Present { value: n }
        JsonNull => none
        JsonBool { value: _ } => none
        JsonString { value: _ } => none
        JsonArray { elements: _ } => none
        JsonObject { members: _ } => none
      }
    JsonMemberAbsent => none
    JsonMemberDuplicated { count: _ } => none
    JsonMemberNotAnObject => none
  }
}

// THE INDEX OF A NAMED IMAGE, AND ITS UNIQUENESS, OVER AN ADMITTED POPULATION (side-chat review
// 5332343434). Every offered row's identity -- one string image_name -- is read BEFORE candidates
// are counted: a row whose image_name is missing, duplicated or not a string could itself be the
// image, so it is not "some other image" but an unread member, and the whole listing is unread.
// Only then is the name counted, and a count above one is ambiguous. Unrelated optional members are
// not required. A listing that names the image twice is ambiguous
// and refuses (side-chat review 5331991982): taking the first match would let the controller's
// enumeration order choose which file is attached. The ambiguity carries every matching row's
// image_index -- the identities the refusal is about -- so it is reported as what it is, a
// well-formed listing offering one name twice, and never folded into an unreadable document; a
// matching row with no numeric image_index is an unread member, exactly as on the unique arm.
type ImageIndexLookup
  = ImageIndexUnique { image_index: String }
  | ImageIndexAbsent
  | ImageIndexAmbiguous { image_indices: List<String> }
  | ImageIndexUnreadable

fn image_index_named(elements: List<JsonValue>, image_name: String) -> ImageIndexLookup {
  let unread = elements |> filter(e => match json_string_member(doc: e, key: "image_name") { Present { value: _ } => false  Absent => true })
  if (unread |> count) > 0 {
    ImageIndexUnreadable
  } else {
    let named = elements |> filter(e => match json_string_member(doc: e, key: "image_name") { Present { value: n } => n == image_name  Absent => false })
    let indices = named |> flat_map(e => match json_number_member(doc: e, key: "image_index") { Present { value: idx } => [idx]  Absent => [] })
    if (indices |> count) < (named |> count) {
      ImageIndexUnreadable
    } else if (named |> count) > 1 {
      ImageIndexAmbiguous { image_indices: indices }
    } else {
      match named.first() {
        Absent => ImageIndexAbsent
        Present { value: e } =>
          match json_number_member(doc: e, key: "image_index") {
            Present { value: idx } => ImageIndexUnique { image_index: idx }
            Absent => ImageIndexUnreadable
          }
      }
    }
  }
}

fn images_array_elements(doc: JsonValue) -> List<JsonValue>? {
  match doc {
    JsonArray { elements: es } => Present { value: es }
    JsonNull => none
    JsonBool { value: _ } => none
    JsonNumber { lexeme: _ } => none
    JsonString { value: _ } => none
    JsonObject { members: _ } => none
  }
}

// THE START-MEDIA BODY, rendered here rather than by the caller so image_redirection cannot be
// omitted by a caller who does not know it is required. extdeps.bmc.megarac records that omitting
// it makes the firmware refuse, a fact that is lost when a body is assembled at a call site.
fn start_media_body(image_name: NonEmptyStr, image_index: String) -> NonEmptyStr {
  join([
    "{\"image_name\":\"", image_name as String,
    "\",\"image_type\":1,\"image_index\":", image_index,
    ",\"image_redirection\":1}"
  ], "") as NonEmptyStr
}

// THE EFFECT SEQUENCE. Session, list, resolve, start, confirm — and the confirmation is a separate
// read rather than the start call's own answer, for the reason given at the top of this module.
//
// THE CREDENTIAL IS A FILE PATH ON EVERY CALL, INCLUDING OpenSession: curl's --data-urlencode
// password@{password_file} reads the form value from the file, so the password never reaches argv
// (extdeps.bmc.megarac OpenSession). Every subsequent operation carries no credential at all
// because the cookie is the bearer.
//
// AN OPENED SESSION WHOSE TOKEN CANNOT BE READ IS STILL AN ALLOCATED SESSION. An earlier
// revision returned SessionReleaseNotAttempted here, which is the leak that saturated this
// controller: OpenSession succeeded, the cookie was written, and CloseSession never ran because
// the renderer treated the arm as "never opened". The DELETE still needs an X-CSRFTOKEN header
// by the upstream contract; the cookie is the bearer, so the header is supplied as a sentinel
// rather than inventing a second CloseSession shape. A refused or uncertain close remains
// SessionReleaseRefused, never NotAttempted. HTTP 401 after CloseSession is evidence the cookie
// no longer authenticates only when the GET presented a parsed X-CSRFTOKEN; a sentinel header
// makes 401 indistinguishable from header rejection (review 67653).
type SessionCsrfStanding
  = SessionCsrfParsed
  | SessionCsrfUnreadable

fn megarac_session_get_writeout_code(get_body: String) -> String {
  match split(s: get_body, delimiter: "\n").last() {
    Present { value: code } => code
    Absent => ""
  }
}

// WHAT ONE COOKIE-BEARING GET ESTABLISHES, AND NOTHING MORE. The probe is a readonly GET on a
// route THIS firmware serves (the remote-media configurations route, which OpenSession's cookie
// succeeds on moments earlier), with the HTTP status as the trailing line. A succeeding GET is a
// session the controller still recognises; a 401 or 403 is a cookie it no longer names -- the
// ABSENCE observation. GET /api/session is NOT that route on this unit: it answers 404 with a live
// cookie (boots 20 and 21, runs 35437393331 and 35445470385), so a 404 here is the route missing,
// not the session, and is refused as unreadable rather than widened into absent. A mid-body code
// with a different trailer is not a status either.
type SessionPresence
  = SessionPresent
  | SessionAbsent { code: String }
  | SessionPresenceUnreadable { detail: String }

fn megarac_session_presence(get_succeeded: Bool, get_body: String) -> SessionPresence {
  if get_succeeded {
    SessionPresent
  } else {
    let code = megarac_session_get_writeout_code(get_body: get_body)
    if code == "401" || code == "403" {
      SessionAbsent { code: code }
    } else {
      SessionPresenceUnreadable { detail: get_body }
    }
  }
}

// RELEASE IS A TRANSITION, NOT A STATUS. A 4xx AFTER CloseSession proves the cookie is gone only
// if the SAME GET succeeded BEFORE CloseSession: a route that 404s regardless of the cookie, or
// a cookie the controller had already dropped, answers 4xx both times and would otherwise read
// as a clean release -- the absorbing fallback DESIGN section 5 forbids, one status code wide.
// So the fold takes both observations and mints SessionReleased for exactly present -> absent.
// ONE REFUSAL VALUE FOR THE SENTINEL-CSRF CASE, consumed by the re-observation fold and by the
// unreadable-token arm that closes without probing (review 68789: the arm had re-typed the sentence).
data megarac_sentinel_csrf_release_refusal: SessionRelease = SessionReleaseRefused { detail: "the session probe around CloseSession used a sentinel X-CSRFTOKEN because the token was unreadable; a refusal here does not prove the cookie is gone" }

fn megarac_session_release_by_reobservation(
  before: SessionPresence,
  after: SessionPresence,
  csrf: SessionCsrfStanding,
) -> SessionRelease {
  match csrf {
    SessionCsrfUnreadable =>
      megarac_sentinel_csrf_release_refusal
    SessionCsrfParsed =>
      match before {
        SessionPresent =>
          match after {
            SessionAbsent { code: _ } => SessionReleased
            SessionPresent => SessionReleaseRefused { detail: "the session probe still succeeded after CloseSession" }
            SessionPresenceUnreadable { detail: d } =>
              SessionReleaseRefused { detail: concat("the session probe after CloseSession was unreadable; refusing to treat the session as released: ", d) }
          }
        SessionAbsent { code: c } =>
          SessionReleaseRefused { detail: concat("the session probe was already refused BEFORE CloseSession (code ", concat(c, "); a refusal after it proves nothing about release -- the route or the cookie was not observable")) }
        SessionPresenceUnreadable { detail: d } =>
          SessionReleaseRefused { detail: concat("the session probe before CloseSession was unreadable; refusing to adjudicate release: ", d) }
      }
  }
}

fn megarac_close_and_reobserve(
  bmc_host: NonEmptyStr,
  cookie_jar: NonEmptyStr,
  csrf_token: NonEmptyStr,
  csrf: SessionCsrfStanding,
) -> SessionRelease
{
  let before_get = megarac.Media.ProbeSessionOnMediaRoute(
    bmc_host: bmc_host,
    cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
    csrf_token: csrf_token,
    max_time: megarac_media_read_max_time_operand(),
  )
  let before = megarac_session_presence(get_succeeded: before_get.success, get_body: before_get.body)
  let _closed = megarac.Media.CloseSession(
    bmc_host: bmc_host,
    cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
    csrf_token: csrf_token,
    max_time: megarac_media_read_max_time_operand(),
  )
  let after_get = megarac.Media.ProbeSessionOnMediaRoute(
    bmc_host: bmc_host,
    cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
    csrf_token: csrf_token,
    max_time: megarac_media_read_max_time_operand(),
  )
  let after = megarac_session_presence(get_succeeded: after_get.success, get_body: after_get.body)
  return megarac_session_release_by_reobservation(before: before, after: after, csrf: csrf)
}

// THE SESSION REPLY'S DECODER, a pure function of the body so a claim supplies the body at this
// interface: the one member read is CSRFToken, and a body that is not a JSON document or lacks it
// reads as absent, which the caller refuses as MegaRacSessionTokenUnreadable.
fn megarac_session_csrf(session_body: String) -> String? {
  let session_doc = match parse_json_document(s: session_body) {
    JsonDocumentParsed { value: v } => some_json_value(v)
    JsonDocumentUnreadable { gap: _ } => none
  }
  return match session_doc {
    Absent => none
    Present { value: doc } => json_string_member(doc: doc, key: "CSRFToken")
  }
}

fn megarac_attach_remote_image(
  bmc_host: NonEmptyStr,
  username: NonEmptyStr,
  password_file: NonEmptyStr,
  cookie_jar: NonEmptyStr,
  image_name: NonEmptyStr,
  firmware: BmcFirmwareReleaseIdentity,
  task: MegaRacSessionTask,
) -> MegaRacAttachResult
  admit_callers: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.machine_intake_megarac_boot_media_attach", decl_name: "megarac_attach_boot_image"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.machine_intake_megarac_boot_media_attach", decl_name: "megarac_observe_boot_presentation"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.machine_intake_megarac_boot_media_attach", decl_name: "megarac_stale_power_off"),
  ]
{
  session = megarac.Media.OpenSession(
    bmc_host: bmc_host,
    username: username,
    password_file: password_file,
    cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
    max_time: megarac_media_read_max_time_operand(),
  )
  if session.success == false {
    return MegaRacAttachResult {
      outcome: MegaRacSessionRefused { detail: session.body },
      session_release: SessionReleaseNotAttempted,
      baseline: none,
    }
  }

  return match megarac_session_csrf(session_body: session.body) {
    Absent =>
      megarac_release_unreadable_session(
        bmc_host: bmc_host,
        cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
        session_body: session.body,
      )
    Present { value: token } =>
      megarac_attach_then_release(
        bmc_host: bmc_host,
        cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
        csrf_token: token as NonEmptyStr,
        image_name: image_name,
        firmware: firmware,
        task: task,
      )
  }
}

// THE CLOSE IS OWED, THE PROBES ARE NOT. With a sentinel X-CSRFTOKEN no probe outcome can prove the
// cookie is gone -- the release fold refuses on SessionCsrfUnreadable before reading either
// observation -- so this arm closes and refuses without spending two round-trips on the one
// transport already known to be misbehaving (review 68750).
fn megarac_release_unreadable_session(
  bmc_host: NonEmptyStr,
  cookie_jar: NonEmptyStr,
  session_body: String,
) -> MegaRacAttachResult
{
  let _closed = megarac.Media.CloseSession(
    bmc_host: bmc_host,
    cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
    csrf_token: "unreadable" as NonEmptyStr,
    max_time: megarac_media_read_max_time_operand(),
  )
  return MegaRacAttachResult {
    outcome: MegaRacSessionTokenUnreadable { detail: session_body },
    session_release: megarac_sentinel_csrf_release_refusal,
    baseline: none,
  }
}

// THE RELEASE RUNS ON EVERY PATH THROUGH THE ATTACH, which is why the attach outcome is computed
// first and the close follows it unconditionally rather than sitting inside a success arm. A
// refusal allocated the same session a success does.
fn megarac_attach_then_release(
  bmc_host: NonEmptyStr,
  cookie_jar: NonEmptyStr,
  csrf_token: NonEmptyStr,
  image_name: NonEmptyStr,
  firmware: BmcFirmwareReleaseIdentity,
  task: MegaRacSessionTask,
) -> MegaRacAttachResult
{
  let converged = match task {
    MegaRacConverge { policy: policy } => {
      let c = megarac_attach_with_token(
        bmc_host: bmc_host,
        cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
        csrf_token: csrf_token,
        image_name: image_name,
        firmware: firmware,
        policy: policy,
      )
      MegaRacConvergence { baseline: c.baseline, outcome: c.outcome }
    }
    MegaRacObserve { share: share } =>
      MegaRacConvergence { baseline: MegaRacMediaBaseline { general_read: false, general: "", configurations_read: false, configurations: "" }, outcome: megarac_observe_with_token(
        bmc_host: bmc_host,
        cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
        csrf_token: csrf_token,
        image_name: image_name,
        firmware: firmware,
        share: share,
      ) }
  }

  let baseline = match task {
    MegaRacConverge { policy: _ } => Present { value: converged.baseline }
    MegaRacObserve { share: _ } => none
  }
  return MegaRacAttachResult {
    outcome: converged.outcome,
    baseline: baseline,
    session_release: megarac_close_and_reobserve(
      bmc_host: bmc_host,
      cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
      csrf_token: csrf_token,
      csrf: SessionCsrfParsed,
    ),
  }
}

// CONFIGURATIONS IS CONSULTED BEFORE ANYTHING IS WRITTEN, so the converged case performs no write
// at all. This is not an optimisation: start-media against an already-presented image is a write
// whose effect on a booted host is unmodelled, and the point of reading first is to not make it.
//
// MALFORMED PRESENTED STATE IS UNKNOWN, NOT "NOT ATTACHED". An earlier revision collapsed a
// JSON parse failure or a non-array document to false, then walked the available-images list
// and could StartMedia over a controller whose current attachment was unreadable. That is the
// absorbing-fallback DESIGN §5 forbids: ignorance rendered as the empty case.
//
// THE SHARE IS READ FIRST, before configurations and before any write, so no route — including
// the no-write already-presented one — can be satisfied by a same-named image from another share.
//
// THE OPERATION IS A CONVERGENCE ON ONE DESIRED IMAGE (operator ruling 2026-09-27: "the workflow
// should be ensuring the correct image"). Boot run 36328950865 refused with the previous census
// image still presented and the new one missing from the listing although it was in the export:
// the rmedia daemon enumerates the share when it mounts it. So the step is: the desired image
// presented goes straight to the readiness fold; another image of the caller's replaceable stem
// presented is stopped, under the caller's admission, and read back as gone; the listing is
// re-read and the desired image's CURRENT index resolved; it is attached; and the attach passes the
// same readiness fold. A presented image outside the replaceable stem is somebody else's and
// refuses.
fn megarac_attach_with_token(
  bmc_host: NonEmptyStr,
  cookie_jar: NonEmptyStr,
  csrf_token: NonEmptyStr,
  image_name: NonEmptyStr,
  firmware: BmcFirmwareReleaseIdentity,
  policy: MegaRacReplacementPolicy,
) -> MegaRacConvergence
{
  let general = megarac.Media.GetMediaGeneral(
    bmc_host: bmc_host,
    cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
    csrf_token: csrf_token,
    max_time: megarac_media_read_max_time_operand(),
  )
  let presented = megarac.Media.GetRemoteConfigurations(
    bmc_host: bmc_host,
    cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
    csrf_token: csrf_token,
    max_time: megarac_media_read_max_time_operand(),
  )
  return MegaRacConvergence {
    baseline: MegaRacMediaBaseline {
      general_read: general.success,
      general: general.body,
      configurations_read: presented.success,
      configurations: presented.body,
    },
    outcome: megarac_converge_from_baseline(
      bmc_host: bmc_host,
      cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
      csrf_token: csrf_token,
      image_name: image_name,
      firmware: firmware,
      policy: policy,
      general_read: general.success,
      general: general.body,
      configurations_read: presented.success,
      configurations: presented.body,
    ),
  }
}

// THE BASELINE IS THE TWO READS TAKEN BEFORE ANY WRITE, kept verbatim in the result whatever
// follows, so every attempt -- and the cd_error_code experiment in particular -- retains what the
// controller said before this attempt touched it.
// ONE READ AS OBSERVED: whether it was answered, the bytes verbatim, and the clock beside it (absent
// when the clock itself could not be read). The cd_error_code experiment is interpreted in time --
// when the code was 16, when 0 -- so every settings read after the baseline keeps its raw bytes and
// its instant rather than only the decoded code (side-chat review 5332343434).
type MegaRacRawRead {
  answered: Bool
  body: String
  observed_at: EpochMs?
}

fn megarac_clock_at() -> EpochMs? {
  match clock_unix_millis_read() {
    ClockUnixMillisObserved { millis: m } => Present { value: m }
    ClockUnixMillisRefused { detail: _ } => none
  }
}

fn megarac_raw_general(bmc_host: NonEmptyStr, cookie_jar: NonEmptyStr, csrf_token: NonEmptyStr) -> MegaRacRawRead {
  let g = megarac.Media.GetMediaGeneral(
    bmc_host: bmc_host,
    cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
    csrf_token: csrf_token,
    max_time: megarac_media_read_max_time_operand(),
  )
  MegaRacRawRead { answered: g.success, body: g.body, observed_at: megarac_clock_at() }
}

fn cd_error_of_raw(r: MegaRacRawRead, firmware: BmcFirmwareReleaseIdentity) -> CdErrorReading {
  if r.answered { cd_error_reading(body: r.body, firmware: firmware) } else { CdErrorUnread { detail: r.body } }
}

type MegaRacMediaBaseline {
  general_read: Bool
  general: String
  configurations_read: Bool
  configurations: String
}

type MegaRacConvergence {
  baseline: MegaRacMediaBaseline
  outcome: MegaRacAttachOutcome
}

fn megarac_converge_from_baseline(
  bmc_host: NonEmptyStr,
  cookie_jar: NonEmptyStr,
  csrf_token: NonEmptyStr,
  image_name: NonEmptyStr,
  firmware: BmcFirmwareReleaseIdentity,
  policy: MegaRacReplacementPolicy,
  general_read: Bool,
  general: String,
  configurations_read: Bool,
  configurations: String,
) -> MegaRacAttachOutcome
{
  if general_read == false {
    return MegaRacShareUnreadable { detail: general }
  }
  match share_binding_standing(body: general, expected: policy.share) {
    ShareUnreadable { detail: d } => return MegaRacShareUnreadable { detail: d }
    ShareMismatch { observed: o } => return MegaRacShareMismatch { expected: policy.share, observed: o }
    ShareBound => none
  }
  let cd_before = cd_error_reading(body: general, firmware: firmware)
  if configurations_read == false {
    return MegaRacConfigurationsUnreadable { detail: configurations }
  }
  let convergence = presented_convergence(
    presented: presented_media(body: configurations, image_name: image_name, firmware: firmware),
    image_name: image_name,
    replaceable_seeded_stem: policy.replaceable_seeded_stem,
  )
  return match megarac_convergence_step(convergence: convergence, detach: policy.detach, configurations: configurations, cd_before: cd_before) {
    ConvergeStepRefuse { outcome: o } => o
    ConvergeStepAwaitReadiness =>
      megarac_readiness_outcome(
        bmc_host: bmc_host,
        cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
        csrf_token: csrf_token,
        image_name: image_name,
        firmware: firmware,
        route: RouteAlreadyPresented,
        phase: ReadinessOfPresented,
        cd_before: cd_before,
      )
    ConvergeStepDetachStale { row: row } =>
      megarac_detach_then_attach(
        bmc_host: bmc_host,
        cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
        csrf_token: csrf_token,
        image_name: image_name,
        firmware: firmware,
        policy: policy,
        stale: row,
        cd_before: cd_before,
      )
    ConvergeStepAttachFromListing =>
      megarac_attach_from_listing(
        bmc_host: bmc_host,
        cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
        csrf_token: csrf_token,
        image_name: image_name,
        firmware: firmware,
        cd_before: cd_before,
      )
  }
}

// EVERY READ IS BOUNDED, not only the window. A configurations or images GET that hangs would
// otherwise hold the readiness window open past its deadline with no look to judge it by, so each
// call carries curl's --max-time and a call that runs out is one unanswered look.
data megarac_media_read_max_time: Second = second(count: 10)

fn megarac_media_read_max_time_operand() -> NonEmptyStr {
  to_string(second_count(s: megarac_media_read_max_time)) as NonEmptyStr
}

// NOTHING PRESENTED: the listing is consulted as before. With nothing presented there is nothing
// to stop, and stopping is what re-enumerates the share, so an image the listing does not offer
// refuses as it always has.
fn megarac_attach_from_listing(
  bmc_host: NonEmptyStr,
  cookie_jar: NonEmptyStr,
  csrf_token: NonEmptyStr,
  image_name: NonEmptyStr,
  firmware: BmcFirmwareReleaseIdentity,
  cd_before: CdErrorReading,
) -> MegaRacAttachOutcome
{
  images = megarac.Media.GetRemoteImages(
    bmc_host: bmc_host,
    cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
    csrf_token: csrf_token,
    max_time: megarac_media_read_max_time_operand(),
  )
  if images.success == false {
    return MegaRacImagesUnreadable { detail: images.body }
  }
  return match images_listing_reading(body: images.body, image_name: image_name) {
    ImagesListingUnparseable { detail: d } => MegaRacImageListingUnparseable { detail: d }
    ImagesListingEmpty => MegaRacImageListingEmpty
    ImagesListingLacks => MegaRacImageNotEnumerated { image_name: image_name }
    ImagesListingOffersAmbiguously { image_indices: ids } => MegaRacImageOfferedAmbiguously { image_name: image_name, image_indices: ids }
    ImagesListingOffers { image_index: idx } =>
      megarac_start_then_readiness(
        bmc_host: bmc_host,
        cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
        csrf_token: csrf_token,
        image_name: image_name,
        image_list_index: idx,
        firmware: firmware,
        detach: none,
        cd_before: cd_before,
      )
  }
}

// THE STOP IS READ BACK BEFORE THE LISTING IS AWAITED, so an attach never follows a stop whose effect
// is unknown. The command's answer and the read-back are both kept (MegaRacDetachEvidence); only the
// read-back decides.
fn megarac_detach_then_attach(
  bmc_host: NonEmptyStr,
  cookie_jar: NonEmptyStr,
  csrf_token: NonEmptyStr,
  image_name: NonEmptyStr,
  firmware: BmcFirmwareReleaseIdentity,
  policy: MegaRacReplacementPolicy,
  stale: PresentingRow,
  cd_before: CdErrorReading,
) -> MegaRacAttachOutcome
{
  let media_index = match stale.media_index {
    Present { value: i } => i
    Absent => ""
  }
  if media_index == "" {
    return MegaRacStaleDetachUnconfirmed {
      detach: MegaRacDetachEvidence {
        stale_image: stale.image_name,
        media_index: "",
        command: WriteNotIssued { reason: "no stop-media body could name the device, so no stop was sent" },
        readback_read: false,
        readback: "",
        cd_after_stop: CdErrorUnread { detail: "no stop was sent" },
        general_after_stop: MegaRacRawRead { answered: false, body: "not read: no stop was sent", observed_at: none },
      },
      reason: "the presenting row carries no media_index, so no stop-media body can name its device; nothing was written",
    }
  }
  let stopped = megarac.Media.StopMedia(
    bmc_host: bmc_host,
    cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
    csrf_token: csrf_token,
    json_body: stop_media_body(image_name: stale.image_name, media_index: media_index),
    max_time: megarac_media_read_max_time_operand(),
  )
  let after = megarac.Media.GetRemoteConfigurations(
    bmc_host: bmc_host,
    cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
    csrf_token: csrf_token,
    max_time: megarac_media_read_max_time_operand(),
  )
  let general_after = megarac_raw_general(bmc_host: bmc_host, cookie_jar: cookie_jar, csrf_token: csrf_token)
  let evidence = MegaRacDetachEvidence {
    stale_image: stale.image_name,
    media_index: media_index,
    command: megarac_write_answer(exit_code: stopped.exit_code, body: stopped.body, stderr: stopped.stderr),
    readback_read: after.success,
    readback: after.body,
    cd_after_stop: cd_error_of_raw(r: general_after, firmware: firmware),
    general_after_stop: general_after,
  }
  return match detach_verdict(evidence: evidence, image_name: image_name, firmware: firmware, replaceable_seeded_stem: policy.replaceable_seeded_stem) {
    DetachNotEstablished { reason: why } => MegaRacStaleDetachUnconfirmed { detach: evidence, reason: why }
    DetachEstablished =>
      megarac_enumerate_then_attach(
        bmc_host: bmc_host,
        cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
        csrf_token: csrf_token,
        image_name: image_name,
        firmware: firmware,
        detach: evidence,
        cd_before: cd_before,
      )
  }
}

type DetachVerdict
  = DetachEstablished
  | DetachNotEstablished { reason: NonEmptyStr }

// PURE: the detach is established exactly when the read-back was read and presents nothing. The
// command's success is not consulted, in either direction.
fn detach_verdict(
  evidence: MegaRacDetachEvidence,
  image_name: NonEmptyStr,
  firmware: BmcFirmwareReleaseIdentity,
  replaceable_seeded_stem: NonEmptyStr,
) -> DetachVerdict {
  if evidence.readback_read == false {
    DetachNotEstablished { reason: "the configurations read-back after stop-media failed, so the stop is unestablished whatever stop-media answered" }
  } else {
    let still_presenting = DetachNotEstablished { reason: "the configurations read-back after stop-media still presents an image, or cannot be read as presenting nothing" }
    match presented_convergence(
      presented: presented_media(body: evidence.readback, image_name: image_name, firmware: firmware),
      image_name: image_name,
      replaceable_seeded_stem: replaceable_seeded_stem,
    ) {
      ConvergeNothingPresented => DetachEstablished
      ConvergeUnreadable { detail: _ } => still_presenting
      ConvergeUncatalogued { image_name: _, wire: _ } => still_presenting
      ConvergeDesiredPresented { row: _ } => still_presenting
      ConvergeStalePresented { row: _ } => still_presenting
      ConvergeForeignPresented { image_name: _ } => still_presenting
      ConvergeSeveralPresented => still_presenting
    }
  }
}

// AN EXECUTED DETACH IS A FACT OF THIS ATTEMPT AND IS NEVER DISCARDED BY A LATER ERROR: every
// outcome reachable after the stop carries its MegaRacDetachEvidence, through its route or its own
// field (side-chat review 5331738657).
//
// STOP-MEDIA IS THE RE-ENUMERATION. Measured on mtcollins1 2026-09-27 with the host off: after
// stop-media cleared the stale presentation, /remote/images listed the newly published census image
// within 15s, while PUT /api/settings/media/general with mount_cd 0 and then 1 was REFUSED both
// times (code 16425, "Error in setting Remote Media Misc Configuration", settings unchanged). So no
// mount_cd cycle is written here: the listing is awaited after the stop, and the index attached is
// the one the CURRENT listing gives the name, never one read before the stop.
fn megarac_enumerate_then_attach(
  bmc_host: NonEmptyStr,
  cookie_jar: NonEmptyStr,
  csrf_token: NonEmptyStr,
  image_name: NonEmptyStr,
  firmware: BmcFirmwareReleaseIdentity,
  detach: MegaRacDetachEvidence,
  cd_before: CdErrorReading,
) -> MegaRacAttachOutcome
{
  return match clock_unix_millis_read() {
    ClockUnixMillisRefused { detail: d } => MegaRacRefreshClockUnreadable { detail: d, detach: detach }
    ClockUnixMillisObserved { millis: requested_at } =>
      match megarac_await_enumeration(
        bmc_host: bmc_host,
        cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
        csrf_token: csrf_token,
        image_name: image_name,
        window: RemoteMediaMountWindow { requested_at: requested_at, budget: megarac_refresh_enumeration_budget_ms() },
        observations: [],
        remaining: megarac_refresh_enumeration_ticks(),
      ) {
        EnumerationClockUnreadable { detail: d } => MegaRacRefreshClockUnreadable { detail: d, detach: detach }
        EnumerationUnparseable { detail: d } => MegaRacListingUnparseableAfterDetach { detail: d, detach: detach }
        EnumerationAmbiguous { image_indices: ids } => MegaRacOfferedAmbiguouslyAfterDetach { image_name: image_name, image_indices: ids, detach: detach }
        NotEnumeratedAfterRefresh { standing: st } => MegaRacNotEnumeratedAfterRefresh { image_name: image_name, detach: detach, standing: st }
        EnumeratedAfterRefresh { image_index: idx } =>
          megarac_start_then_readiness(
            bmc_host: bmc_host,
            cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
            csrf_token: csrf_token,
            image_name: image_name,
            image_list_index: idx,
            firmware: firmware,
            detach: Present { value: detach },
            cd_before: cd_before,
          )
      }
  }
}

// THE STOP-MEDIA BODY. extdeps.bmc.megarac records only that stop-media takes start-media's body
// shape; which index it wants is not recorded anywhere, so this is a typed bet rather than a fact:
// the row's media_index, the virtual device the presentation occupies, since the image enumeration
// index of an attached image is not listed (it has left /remote/images). The read-back decides
// whether the bet held; a wrong index is StaleDetachUnconfirmed, never a success.
fn stop_media_body(image_name: String, media_index: String) -> NonEmptyStr {
  join([
    "{\"image_name\":\"", image_name,
    "\",\"image_type\":1,\"image_index\":", media_index,
    ",\"image_redirection\":1}"
  ], "") as NonEmptyStr
}

// THE RE-ENUMERATION IS A BOUNDED ESTABLISHMENT, folded by gunbc.machine_intake_mount_establishment
// rather than polled until green: the window is declared before the first look, each look is an
// evidenced observation, and a close at the deadline is terminal. The budget is the controller's
// configured retry cadence with margin: rmedia_retry_count 3 at rmedia_retry_interval 15s is 45s,
// and the measured re-enumeration after stop-media took under 15s (2026-09-27).
data megarac_refresh_poll_interval: Second = second(count: 5)

data megarac_refresh_enumeration_budget: Second = second(count: 90)

fn megarac_refresh_enumeration_budget_ms() -> Milliseconds {
  (second_count(s: megarac_refresh_enumeration_budget) as Int) * 1000
}

// One look per interval across the window, plus the look that lands at or past the deadline and
// closes it, so running out of ticks before the window closes is not a reachable exit.
fn megarac_refresh_enumeration_ticks() -> Int {
  (second_count(s: megarac_refresh_enumeration_budget) as Int) / (second_count(s: megarac_refresh_poll_interval) as Int) + 2
}

// ONE READ-ONLY LOOK: session open, the general and configurations reads, the close and its two
// probes -- six bounded calls. A caller that takes looks around its own effects budgets them with this.
fn megarac_presentation_look_allowance() -> Second {
  second(count: 6 * (second_count(s: megarac_media_read_max_time) as Int))
}

// THE BOUNDED CALLS OF THE LONGEST CONVERGENCE ROUTE (replace a stale image, then attach), each
// capped by megarac_media_read_max_time: OpenSession; the baseline GetMediaGeneral and
// GetRemoteConfigurations; StopMedia; its configurations read-back and its GetMediaGeneral; StartMedia;
// the GetMediaGeneral at the end of the readiness wait; and the release -- ProbeSessionOnMediaRoute,
// CloseSession, ProbeSessionOnMediaRoute. Eleven. The two waits' looks are bounded by their own
// windows plus one pacing interval and one last bounded read each.
data megarac_convergence_fixed_calls: Int = 11

// WHAT THE WHOLE CONVERGENCE MAY SPEND, DERIVED from the route above rather than padded: both windows,
// each window's last pacing interval and last bounded read, and every fixed call at its bound.
fn megarac_convergence_allowance() -> Second {
  let read = second_count(s: megarac_media_read_max_time) as Int
  second(count: (second_count(s: megarac_refresh_enumeration_budget) as Int) + (second_count(s: megarac_refresh_poll_interval) as Int) + read
    + (second_count(s: megarac_readiness_budget) as Int) + (second_count(s: megarac_readiness_interval) as Int) + read
    + megarac_convergence_fixed_calls * read)
}

type EnumerationAfterRefresh
  = EnumeratedAfterRefresh { image_index: String }
  | NotEnumeratedAfterRefresh { standing: RemoteMediaMountStanding }
  | EnumerationUnparseable { detail: String }
  | EnumerationAmbiguous { image_indices: List<String> }
  | EnumerationClockUnreadable { detail: String }

// A LISTING THAT REFUSES IS PENDING, A LISTING THAT PARSES AND LACKS THE NAME IS ABSENT, AND BOTH
// ARE ONE MISS INSIDE THE WINDOW. extdeps.bmc.megarac records that "Could not mount the remote
// path" on the images route means the daemon has not mounted yet; a body that answers but is not a
// JSON array is a protocol failure and refuses at once. The first look is taken at once; the pacing
// sleep runs only between looks that were still pending.
fn megarac_await_enumeration(
  bmc_host: NonEmptyStr,
  cookie_jar: NonEmptyStr,
  csrf_token: NonEmptyStr,
  image_name: NonEmptyStr,
  window: RemoteMediaMountWindow,
  observations: List<RemoteMediaListingObservation>,
  remaining: Int,
) -> EnumerationAfterRefresh
{
  let images = megarac.Media.GetRemoteImages(
    bmc_host: bmc_host,
    cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
    csrf_token: csrf_token,
    max_time: megarac_media_read_max_time_operand(),
  )
  let reading = if images.success { images_listing_reading(body: images.body, image_name: image_name) } else { ImagesListingLacks }
  match clock_unix_millis_read() {
    ClockUnixMillisRefused { detail: d } => EnumerationClockUnreadable { detail: d }
    ClockUnixMillisObserved { millis: now } => {
      let step = match reading {
        ImagesListingUnparseable { detail: d } => ListedEnumerationDone { result: EnumerationUnparseable { detail: d } }
        ImagesListingOffersAmbiguously { image_indices: ids } => ListedEnumerationDone { result: EnumerationAmbiguous { image_indices: ids } }
        ImagesListingEmpty => megarac_listed_enumeration_step(body: images.body, reading: reading, now: now, window: window, observations: observations, remaining: remaining)
        ImagesListingLacks => megarac_listed_enumeration_step(body: images.body, reading: reading, now: now, window: window, observations: observations, remaining: remaining)
        ImagesListingOffers { image_index: _ } => megarac_listed_enumeration_step(body: images.body, reading: reading, now: now, window: window, observations: observations, remaining: remaining)
      }
      match step {
        ListedEnumerationDone { result: r } => r
        ListedEnumerationLookAgain { observations: seen } => {
          let _paced = sleep_delay_seconds_second_carrier_projection(duration: megarac_refresh_poll_interval)
          megarac_await_enumeration(
            bmc_host: bmc_host,
            cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
            csrf_token: csrf_token,
            image_name: image_name,
            window: window,
            observations: seen,
            remaining: remaining - 1,
          )
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

// One look's conclusion for a listing that parsed: the loop's self tail-call stays in
// megarac_await_enumeration, which matches this step exhaustively.
type ListedEnumerationStep
  = ListedEnumerationDone { result: EnumerationAfterRefresh }
  | ListedEnumerationLookAgain { observations: List<RemoteMediaListingObservation> }

fn megarac_listed_enumeration_step(
  body: String,
  reading: ImagesListingReading,
  now: EpochMs,
  window: RemoteMediaMountWindow,
  observations: List<RemoteMediaListingObservation>,
  remaining: Int,
) -> ListedEnumerationStep {
  let evidence = content_hash_of_value(value: concat("megarac-remote-images:", body) as NonEmptyStr)
  let seen = observations.append(RemoteMediaListingObservation {
    observed_at: now,
    listing: images_listing_presence(reading: reading),
    raw_response: evidence,
  })
  let standing = mount_standing_as_of(
    window: window,
    observations: seen,
    boundary: MountEvaluationBoundary { observed_through: now, clock_evidence: evidence },
  )
  return match enumeration_decision(standing: standing, reading: reading, remaining: remaining) {
    EnumerationDecided { result: r } => ListedEnumerationDone { result: r }
    EnumerationLookAgain => ListedEnumerationLookAgain { observations: seen }
  }
}

type EnumerationDecision
  = EnumerationDecided { result: EnumerationAfterRefresh }
  | EnumerationLookAgain

// ONLY THE FOLD'S ESTABLISHED STANDING ATTACHES, and only with the index the establishing look read.
// Pending inside the window looks again; every terminal standing is NotEnumeratedAfterRefresh and
// carries the standing that closed it, so a contradiction is reported as one rather than as a miss.
fn enumeration_decision(standing: RemoteMediaMountStanding, reading: ImagesListingReading, remaining: Int) -> EnumerationDecision {
  match standing {
    MountEstablished { established_at: _, establishing_evidence: _ } =>
      match reading {
        ImagesListingOffers { image_index: idx } => EnumerationDecided { result: EnumeratedAfterRefresh { image_index: idx } }
        ImagesListingUnparseable { detail: _ } => EnumerationDecided { result: NotEnumeratedAfterRefresh { standing: standing } }
        ImagesListingEmpty => EnumerationDecided { result: NotEnumeratedAfterRefresh { standing: standing } }
        ImagesListingLacks => EnumerationDecided { result: NotEnumeratedAfterRefresh { standing: standing } }
        ImagesListingOffersAmbiguously { image_indices: ids } => EnumerationDecided { result: EnumerationAmbiguous { image_indices: ids } }
      }
    MountRequested { window: _ } =>
      if remaining > 1 { EnumerationLookAgain } else { EnumerationDecided { result: NotEnumeratedAfterRefresh { standing: standing } } }
    MountPending { window: _, last_observed_at: _, observations: _ } =>
      if remaining > 1 { EnumerationLookAgain } else { EnumerationDecided { result: NotEnumeratedAfterRefresh { standing: standing } } }
    MountTimedOut { window: _, basis: _ } => EnumerationDecided { result: NotEnumeratedAfterRefresh { standing: standing } }
    MountObservationContradictory { cause: _ } => EnumerationDecided { result: NotEnumeratedAfterRefresh { standing: standing } }
  }
}

// THE AVAILABLE-TO-ATTACH LISTING, read once. It lists what may be attached, not what the share
// holds: an attached image has moved to /remote/configurations (see the top of this module).
type ImagesListingReading
  = ImagesListingUnparseable { detail: String }
  | ImagesListingEmpty
  | ImagesListingLacks
  | ImagesListingOffers { image_index: String }
  | ImagesListingOffersAmbiguously { image_indices: List<String> }

fn images_listing_reading(body: String, image_name: NonEmptyStr) -> ImagesListingReading {
  match parse_json_document(s: body) {
    JsonDocumentUnreadable { gap: _ } => ImagesListingUnparseable { detail: body }
    JsonDocumentParsed { value: v } =>
      match images_array_elements(doc: v) {
        Absent => ImagesListingUnparseable { detail: body }
        Present { value: elements } =>
          if (elements |> count) == 0 {
            ImagesListingEmpty
          } else {
            match image_index_named(elements: elements, image_name: image_name as String) {
              ImageIndexAbsent => ImagesListingLacks
              ImageIndexUnique { image_index: idx } => ImagesListingOffers { image_index: idx }
              ImageIndexAmbiguous { image_indices: ids } => ImagesListingOffersAmbiguously { image_indices: ids }
              ImageIndexUnreadable => ImagesListingUnparseable { detail: concat("the listing has a row without one readable string image_name, or names the image without a numeric image_index: ", body) }
            }
          }
      }
  }
}

// A name offered twice IS listed; the await loop refuses on the ambiguity before any look reaches the
// mount standing, so this arm states presence and decides nothing.
fn images_listing_presence(reading: ImagesListingReading) -> RemoteMediaListing {
  match reading {
    ImagesListingOffers { image_index: _ } => MediaImageListed
    ImagesListingUnparseable { detail: _ } => MediaImageAbsentFromListing
    ImagesListingEmpty => MediaImageAbsentFromListing
    ImagesListingLacks => MediaImageAbsentFromListing
    ImagesListingOffersAmbiguously { image_indices: _ } => MediaImageListed
  }
}

// ONE PRESENTING ROW: this CD device is presenting this name, with redirection started or
// connecting. media_index is the virtual device slot, carried for the stop-media body only and
// never compared against an image index (the nicknaming note on configuration_row_reading).
type PresentingRow {
  image_name: String
  media_index: String?
  session_index: String?
  redirection_wire: Int
  redirection: MegaRacRedirectionStatus
}

// THE CONFIRMATION READS EXACT ACTIVE ROWS, not a substring of a body. An earlier form asked
// whether the configurations text CONTAINED the image name, which admits a stopped configuration
// that still names it, and admits an error body that happens to mention it.
//
// THE INDEX IS DELIBERATELY NOT COMPARED, and an earlier revision of this check did compare it —
// first reading image_index, which is absent here so every genuine attachment was reported
// unconfirmed, then reading media_index, which is present and agrees. The second spelling passed,
// and it was still wrong: media_index is the VIRTUAL CD DEVICE SLOT, alongside session_index, not a
// position in the image enumeration. It agreed with the resolved image_index only because this unit
// presents a single CD device, so both are 0. Comparing them is the §3 nicknaming failure — two
// unrelated concepts joined because they share a coincidence and half a name — and it would have
// started refusing the moment a controller offered a second slot, with a message blaming the image.
//
// EVERY ROW IS READ, NOT ONLY THE ONE NAMING THE DESIRED IMAGE, AND ONLY A WELL-FORMED ROW IS IDLE
// (side-chat review 5331738657). A row is idle exactly when it carries one string image_name, one
// numeric media_type and one numeric redirection_status, and is either a known-stopped CD row or a
// non-CD row naming some other image. Anything else -- `{}`, a missing, duplicated or wrongly typed
// member, an uncatalogued status whether or not the row names an image -- is unread, and one unread
// row makes the whole document unreadable, so a valid Started row beside it establishes neither
// readiness nor a detach. The observed cleared rows (image_name "", status 0) are well-formed and
// idle, which is what lets a real stop establish.
type ConfigurationRowReading
  = ConfigurationRowUnreadable { detail: String }
  | ConfigurationRowUncatalogued { image_name: String, wire: Int }
  | ConfigurationRowPresenting { row: PresentingRow }
  | ConfigurationRowIdle

fn configuration_row_reading(
  row: JsonValue,
  image_name: NonEmptyStr,
  firmware: BmcFirmwareReleaseIdentity,
) -> ConfigurationRowReading {
  match json_string_member(doc: row, key: "image_name") {
    Absent => ConfigurationRowUnreadable { detail: "a configurations row has no single string image_name (missing, duplicated or not a string)" }
    Present { value: name } =>
      match json_number_member(doc: row, key: "media_type") {
        Absent => ConfigurationRowUnreadable { detail: concat("a configurations row has no single numeric media_type; image_name '", concat(name, "'")) }
        Present { value: mt } =>
          match json_number_member(doc: row, key: "redirection_status") {
            Absent => ConfigurationRowUnreadable { detail: concat("a configurations row has no single numeric redirection_status; image_name '", concat(name, "'")) }
            Present { value: st } =>
              match parse_int(s: st) {
                Absent => ConfigurationRowUnreadable { detail: concat("redirection_status is not an integer: ", st) }
                Present { value: wire } =>
                  if mt != "1" {
                    if name == (image_name as String) {
                      ConfigurationRowUnreadable { detail: "a row names the image but is not CD media_type 1" }
                    } else {
                      ConfigurationRowIdle
                    }
                  } else {
                    match megarac_redirection_status_of_wire(firmware: firmware, wire: wire) {
                      RedirectionStatusFirmwareUncatalogued { firmware: _, wire: w } => ConfigurationRowUncatalogued { image_name: name, wire: w }
                      RedirectionStatusKnown { firmware: _, status: status } =>
                        match status {
                          RedirectionStopped => ConfigurationRowIdle
                          RedirectionWireUncatalogued { wire: w } => ConfigurationRowUncatalogued { image_name: name, wire: w }
                          RedirectionStartedConnectionAccepted => configuration_row_presenting_reading(row: row, name: name, wire: wire, status: status)
                          RedirectionConnecting => configuration_row_presenting_reading(row: row, name: name, wire: wire, status: status)
                        }
                    }
                  }
              }
          }
      }
  }
}

fn configuration_row_presenting_reading(
  row: JsonValue,
  name: String,
  wire: Int,
  status: MegaRacRedirectionStatus,
) -> ConfigurationRowReading {
  if name == "" {
    ConfigurationRowUnreadable { detail: "a CD row is presenting but names no image" }
  } else {
    ConfigurationRowPresenting {
      row: PresentingRow {
        image_name: name,
        media_index: json_number_member(doc: row, key: "media_index"),
        session_index: json_number_member(doc: row, key: "session_index"),
        redirection_wire: wire,
        redirection: status,
      },
    }
  }
}

type PresentedMedia
  = PresentedMediaDocumentUnreadable { detail: String }
  | PresentedMediaUncatalogued { image_name: String, wire: Int }
  | PresentedMediaRead { presenting: List<PresentingRow> }

fn presented_media(
  body: String,
  image_name: NonEmptyStr,
  firmware: BmcFirmwareReleaseIdentity,
) -> PresentedMedia {
  match parse_json_document(s: body) {
    JsonDocumentUnreadable { gap: _ } => PresentedMediaDocumentUnreadable { detail: body }
    JsonDocumentParsed { value: v } =>
      match images_array_elements(doc: v) {
        Absent => PresentedMediaDocumentUnreadable { detail: body }
        Present { value: rows } =>
          fold(rows, init: PresentedMediaRead { presenting: [] }, f: (acc, row) =>
            match acc {
              PresentedMediaDocumentUnreadable { detail: _ } => acc
              PresentedMediaUncatalogued { image_name: _, wire: _ } => acc
              PresentedMediaRead { presenting: ps } =>
                match configuration_row_reading(row: row, image_name: image_name, firmware: firmware) {
                  ConfigurationRowUnreadable { detail: d } => PresentedMediaDocumentUnreadable { detail: d }
                  ConfigurationRowUncatalogued { image_name: n, wire: w } => PresentedMediaUncatalogued { image_name: n, wire: w }
                  ConfigurationRowIdle => acc
                  ConfigurationRowPresenting { row: r } => PresentedMediaRead { presenting: ps.append(r) }
                }
            }
          )
      }
  }
}

// WHAT IS PRESENTED, RELATIVE TO THE DESIRED IMAGE AND THE REPLACEABLE STEM. The desired image
// presented goes to the readiness fold, which is where duplicate or mixed rows are judged.
// Otherwise any presented image the stem's naming inverse does not recognise is foreign and
// decides the answer; this unit presents one CD device, so two replaceable images presented at
// once is a state never observed and refuses rather than being stopped in some order.
type PresentedConvergence
  = ConvergeUnreadable { detail: String }
  | ConvergeUncatalogued { image_name: String, wire: Int }
  | ConvergeDesiredPresented { row: PresentingRow }
  | ConvergeNothingPresented
  | ConvergeStalePresented { row: PresentingRow }
  | ConvergeForeignPresented { image_name: String }
  | ConvergeSeveralPresented

fn presented_convergence(
  presented: PresentedMedia,
  image_name: NonEmptyStr,
  replaceable_seeded_stem: NonEmptyStr,
) -> PresentedConvergence {
  match presented {
    PresentedMediaDocumentUnreadable { detail: d } => ConvergeUnreadable { detail: d }
    PresentedMediaUncatalogued { image_name: n, wire: w } => ConvergeUncatalogued { image_name: n, wire: w }
    PresentedMediaRead { presenting: ps } => presented_population_convergence(presenting: ps, image_name: image_name, replaceable_seeded_stem: replaceable_seeded_stem)
  }
}

// THE WHOLE POPULATION IS CLASSIFIED BEFORE ANY ROW IS CHOSEN (side-chat review 5331991982). The
// presenting rows are partitioned into desired, other census images of the stem, and foreign; the
// answer depends on the counts, never on row order, so no StopMedia index can come from whichever
// row the controller listed first. Any foreign row refuses. More than one presenting row of any
// kind -- two desired, desired beside a census image, two census images -- is ambiguous on a
// single-CD unit and refuses. Only a population of exactly one row names the row a write may use.
fn presented_population_convergence(
  presenting: List<PresentingRow>,
  image_name: NonEmptyStr,
  replaceable_seeded_stem: NonEmptyStr,
) -> PresentedConvergence {
  let desired = presenting |> filter(r => r.image_name == (image_name as String))
  let others = presenting |> filter(r => r.image_name != (image_name as String))
  let foreign = others |> filter(r => match ubuntu_seeded_install_media_name_digest_prefix(image_stem: replaceable_seeded_stem, image_name: r.image_name) { Absent => true  Present { value: _ } => false })
  if (foreign |> count) > 0 {
    match foreign.first() {
      Present { value: f } => ConvergeForeignPresented { image_name: f.image_name }
      Absent => ConvergeSeveralPresented
    }
  } else if (presenting |> count) > 1 {
    ConvergeSeveralPresented
  } else {
    match desired.first() {
      Present { value: d } => ConvergeDesiredPresented { row: d }
      Absent =>
        match others.first() {
          Present { value: o } => ConvergeStalePresented { row: o }
          Absent => ConvergeNothingPresented
        }
    }
  }
}

type ConvergenceStep
  = ConvergeStepAwaitReadiness
  | ConvergeStepRefuse { outcome: MegaRacAttachOutcome }
  | ConvergeStepDetachStale { row: PresentingRow }
  | ConvergeStepAttachFromListing

// THE DECISION, PURE, so every control is a supplied configurations reading rather than a
// controller. THE CODE'S DISPOSITION IS EXPLICIT ON EVERY ROUTE (side-chat review 5331991982), and
// follows the vendor's UI: the desired image presented (Started or connecting) goes to the no-write
// readiness fold whatever the code reads, because the vendor does not consult it then; nothing
// presented is attached on a clean code or a named stop reason (the vendor's stopped view leaves Start
// enabled), and on a code outside the table only under the fresh-presentation admission; an UNREAD
// code never licenses a write. The admission is read only on the arms that would write.
fn megarac_convergence_step(
  convergence: PresentedConvergence,
  detach: MegaRacDetachAdmission,
  configurations: String,
  cd_before: CdErrorReading,
) -> ConvergenceStep {
  match convergence {
    ConvergeUnreadable { detail: d } => ConvergeStepRefuse { outcome: MegaRacConfigurationsUnreadable { detail: d } }
    ConvergeUncatalogued { image_name: n, wire: w } => ConvergeStepRefuse { outcome: MegaRacRedirectionUncatalogued { image_name: n, wire: w, configurations: configurations } }
    ConvergeForeignPresented { image_name: n } => ConvergeStepRefuse { outcome: MegaRacForeignImagePresented { image_name: n, configurations: configurations } }
    ConvergeSeveralPresented => ConvergeStepRefuse { outcome: MegaRacSeveralImagesPresented { configurations: configurations } }
    ConvergeDesiredPresented { row: _ } => ConvergeStepAwaitReadiness
    ConvergeStalePresented { row: r } =>
      match cd_before {
        CdErrorUnread { detail: _ } => ConvergeStepRefuse { outcome: unestablished_before_write(cd_before: cd_before, reason: "cd_error_code could not be read, and an unknown media state never licenses withdrawing a presentation") }
        CdErrorRead { code: _ } =>
          match detach {
            MegaRacDetachAdmitted => ConvergeStepDetachStale { row: r }
            MegaRacDetachNotAdmitted { reason: why } => ConvergeStepRefuse { outcome: MegaRacStaleDetachNotAdmitted { stale_image: r.image_name, reason: why } }
          }
      }
    ConvergeNothingPresented =>
      match cd_before {
        CdErrorRead { code: CdErrorNone } => ConvergeStepAttachFromListing
        CdErrorUnread { detail: _ } => ConvergeStepRefuse { outcome: unestablished_before_write(cd_before: cd_before, reason: "cd_error_code could not be read, so this attempt cannot establish the media state it would attach into") }
        CdErrorRead { code: c } =>
          match cd_error_attach_policy_admits(code: c) {
            true => ConvergeStepAttachFromListing
            false =>
              match detach {
                MegaRacDetachAdmitted => ConvergeStepAttachFromListing
                MegaRacDetachNotAdmitted { reason: why } => ConvergeStepRefuse { outcome: unestablished_before_write(cd_before: cd_before, reason: concat("nothing is presented, cd_error_code is nonzero, and the fresh-presentation experiment was not admitted: ", why as String)) }
              }
          }
      }
  }
}

fn unestablished_before_write(cd_before: CdErrorReading, reason: String) -> MegaRacAttachOutcome {
  MegaRacMediaStateUnestablishedBeforeWrite { cd_before_any_write: cd_before, reason: reason as NonEmptyStr }
}

// A NON-ZERO START IS NOT A REFUSAL, and this firmware is why: the same controller answers HTTP 500
// on writes that take effect, and its mount daemon is asynchronous. The readiness fold decides.
fn megarac_start_then_readiness(
  bmc_host: NonEmptyStr,
  cookie_jar: NonEmptyStr,
  csrf_token: NonEmptyStr,
  image_name: NonEmptyStr,
  image_list_index: String,
  firmware: BmcFirmwareReleaseIdentity,
  detach: MegaRacDetachEvidence?,
  cd_before: CdErrorReading,
) -> MegaRacAttachOutcome
{
  let started = megarac.Media.StartMedia(
    bmc_host: bmc_host,
    cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
    csrf_token: csrf_token,
    json_body: start_media_body(image_name: image_name, image_index: image_list_index),
    max_time: megarac_media_read_max_time_operand(),
  )
  let start = megarac_write_answer(exit_code: started.exit_code, body: started.body, stderr: started.stderr)
  return megarac_readiness_outcome(
    bmc_host: bmc_host,
    cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
    csrf_token: csrf_token,
    image_name: image_name,
    firmware: firmware,
    route: match detach {
      Absent => RouteAttached { image_list_index: image_list_index, start: start }
      Present { value: d } => RouteReplaced { image_list_index: image_list_index, detach: d, start: start }
    },
    phase: ReadinessAfterStart,
    cd_before: cd_before,
  )
}

// ─── READINESS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// THE POLICY, AND WHY IT IS NOT THE FIRMWARE'S STATE. Boot run 36330382023 read configurations
// 0.11s after start-media and powered on 0.7s later; the firmware printed "Boot option loading
// failed" and fell to the UEFI shell, and configurations afterwards read status 16, session_index
// 255. So the POLICY here is: only STARTED, on exactly one CD row naming the intended image, with a
// bound session, is ready. CONNECTING is pending and is observed again within the window. That is a
// readiness policy, not a claim that 100 never serves: a boot on this unit once reached GRUB from a
// session that still read 100 (extdeps.bmc.megarac megarac_redirection_presentation_standing keeps
// Connecting as presenting, and this does not redefine it). The manual re-attach of 2026-09-27 read
// 100 at +6s and 1 with session_index 0 from +12s, stable to +120s, so waiting for Started costs
// seconds and buys the state a boot is known to succeed from.
//
// NOT PRESENTED is pending only after this attempt's own start-media — the admitted establishment
// transition. On the already-presented route the row was just seen, so its disappearance is a
// withdrawal nobody here requested and refuses.
//
// UNCATALOGUED, MALFORMED, AMBIGUOUS OR WRONG refuse at once with the evidence: an uncatalogued
// wire keeps its number, duplicate rows naming the image and a row presenting a different image
// keep the configurations document. Decoder ignorance is not a retry cue.
type ReadinessPhase
  = ReadinessAfterStart
  | ReadinessOfPresented

type AttachReadiness
  = ReadinessStarted { row: PresentingRow }
  | ReadinessConnecting { row: PresentingRow }
  | ReadinessStartedUnbound { row: PresentingRow }
  | ReadinessNotPresented { configurations: String }
  | ReadinessUnanswered { detail: String }
  | ReadinessUncatalogued { image_name: String, wire: Int, configurations: String }
  | ReadinessMalformed { detail: String }
  | ReadinessDuplicate { configurations: String }
  | ReadinessWrongPresentation { image_name: String, configurations: String }

type ReadinessLook {
  observed_at: EpochMs
  reading: AttachReadiness
}

// THE SESSION IS BOUND WHEN session_index NAMES A SLOT. 255 is what the failed boot's row carried
// beside status 16, and an unsigned byte at its maximum is the usual "no slot" sentinel; that it
// means unbound on this firmware is a typed bet from one observation, not a documented fact, and
// it errs toward waiting rather than toward powering on.
data megarac_unbound_session_index: Int = 255

fn presenting_session_bound(row: PresentingRow) -> Bool {
  match row.session_index {
    Absent => false
    Present { value: s } =>
      match parse_int(s: s) {
        Absent => false
        Present { value: n } => n >= 0 && n < megarac_unbound_session_index
      }
  }
}

// ONE LOOK, PURE, over one configurations answer, so every control is a supplied body.
fn attach_readiness(
  answered: Bool,
  body: String,
  image_name: NonEmptyStr,
  firmware: BmcFirmwareReleaseIdentity,
) -> AttachReadiness {
  if answered == false {
    ReadinessUnanswered { detail: body }
  } else {
    match presented_media(body: body, image_name: image_name, firmware: firmware) {
      PresentedMediaDocumentUnreadable { detail: d } => ReadinessMalformed { detail: d }
      PresentedMediaUncatalogued { image_name: n, wire: w } => ReadinessUncatalogued { image_name: n, wire: w, configurations: body }
      PresentedMediaRead { presenting: ps } => {
        let named = ps |> filter(r => r.image_name == (image_name as String))
        let others = ps |> filter(r => r.image_name != (image_name as String))
        if (others |> count) > 0 {
          match others.first() {
            Present { value: o } => ReadinessWrongPresentation { image_name: o.image_name, configurations: body }
            Absent => ReadinessMalformed { detail: body }
          }
        } else if (named |> count) > 1 {
          ReadinessDuplicate { configurations: body }
        } else {
          match named.first() {
            Absent => ReadinessNotPresented { configurations: body }
            Present { value: r } =>
              match r.redirection {
                RedirectionStartedConnectionAccepted =>
                  if presenting_session_bound(row: r) { ReadinessStarted { row: r } } else { ReadinessStartedUnbound { row: r } }
                RedirectionStopped => ReadinessConnecting { row: r }
                RedirectionConnecting => ReadinessConnecting { row: r }
                RedirectionWireUncatalogued { wire: _ } => ReadinessConnecting { row: r }
              }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

type ReadinessStanding
  = ReadinessEstablished { look: ReadinessLook }
  | ReadinessPending
  | ReadinessRefusedAt { look: ReadinessLook }

// THE ONE-LOOK STANDING, pure. Pending is representable only for readings the policy calls
// transitional, and not-presented only in the start phase. An unanswered GET (curl ran out of its
// --max-time, or the controller answered 5xx mid-transition) is one miss, not evidence either way.
fn readiness_standing(look: ReadinessLook, phase: ReadinessPhase) -> ReadinessStanding {
  match look.reading {
    ReadinessStarted { row: _ } => ReadinessEstablished { look: look }
    ReadinessConnecting { row: _ } => ReadinessPending
    ReadinessStartedUnbound { row: _ } => ReadinessPending
    ReadinessUnanswered { detail: _ } => ReadinessPending
    ReadinessNotPresented { configurations: _ } =>
      match phase {
        ReadinessAfterStart => ReadinessPending
        ReadinessOfPresented => ReadinessRefusedAt { look: look }
      }
    ReadinessUncatalogued { image_name: _, wire: _, configurations: _ } => ReadinessRefusedAt { look: look }
    ReadinessMalformed { detail: _ } => ReadinessRefusedAt { look: look }
    ReadinessDuplicate { configurations: _ } => ReadinessRefusedAt { look: look }
    ReadinessWrongPresentation { image_name: _, configurations: _ } => ReadinessRefusedAt { look: look }
  }
}

type ReadinessVerdict
  = ReadinessReady { look: ReadinessLook, looks: Int }
  | ReadinessLookAgain
  | ReadinessWindowClosed { last: ReadinessLook, deadline: EpochMs, looks: Int }
  | ReadinessRefusedVerdict { look: ReadinessLook, looks: Int }
  | ReadinessClockIncoherent { opened_at: EpochMs, previous: EpochMs?, look: ReadinessLook, looks: Int }

// THE WINDOW IS HALF-OPEN AND DECLARED BEFORE THE FIRST LOOK: opened_at <= observed_at < deadline,
// and it is ENFORCED at both ends (side-chat review 5331738657). A look stamped before the window
// opened, or not strictly after the previous look (the wait sleeps between looks, so an equal or
// earlier reading is a stalled or backward clock), is a clock that cannot bound this wait: it is
// ReadinessClockIncoherent, kept with its readings, never judged as ready or pending. The look count
// is an independent bound, so a clock that never advances cannot hold the wait open either. A
// Started look at or past the deadline is outside the window and does not establish readiness; a
// refusal reading refuses whenever it is seen inside a coherent clock.
fn readiness_verdict(
  opened_at: EpochMs,
  budget: Milliseconds,
  previous: EpochMs?,
  look: ReadinessLook,
  phase: ReadinessPhase,
  looks: Int,
) -> ReadinessVerdict {
  let deadline = opened_at + budget
  let backward = match previous { Present { value: p } => look.observed_at <= p  Absent => false }
  if look.observed_at < opened_at || backward {
    ReadinessClockIncoherent { opened_at: opened_at, previous: previous, look: look, looks: looks }
  } else {
    match readiness_standing(look: look, phase: phase) {
      ReadinessRefusedAt { look: l } => ReadinessRefusedVerdict { look: l, looks: looks }
      ReadinessEstablished { look: l } =>
        if l.observed_at < deadline { ReadinessReady { look: l, looks: looks } } else { ReadinessWindowClosed { last: l, deadline: deadline, looks: looks } }
      ReadinessPending =>
        if look.observed_at < deadline && looks < megarac_readiness_max_looks() { ReadinessLookAgain } else { ReadinessWindowClosed { last: look, deadline: deadline, looks: looks } }
    }
  }
}

// The window's looks at the pacing interval, plus the look that reaches the deadline.
fn megarac_readiness_max_looks() -> Int {
  (second_count(s: megarac_readiness_budget) as Int) / (second_count(s: megarac_readiness_interval) as Int) + 1
}

data megarac_readiness_budget: Second = second(count: 30)

data megarac_readiness_interval: Second = second(count: 2)

fn megarac_readiness_budget_ms() -> Milliseconds {
  (second_count(s: megarac_readiness_budget) as Int) * 1000
}

type ReadinessWait
  = ReadinessWaitReady { look: ReadinessLook, looks: Int }
  | ReadinessWaitClosed { last: ReadinessLook, deadline: EpochMs, looks: Int }
  | ReadinessWaitRefused { look: ReadinessLook, looks: Int }
  | ReadinessWaitClockUnreadable { detail: String }
  | ReadinessWaitClockIncoherent { opened_at: EpochMs, previous: EpochMs?, look: ReadinessLook, looks: Int }

// THE WAIT: read at once, and pace only between looks that were pending. The window is judged by the
// clock read beside each look; each look's GET is bounded by --max-time, so no single call can hold
// the window open.
fn megarac_await_readiness(
  bmc_host: NonEmptyStr,
  cookie_jar: NonEmptyStr,
  csrf_token: NonEmptyStr,
  image_name: NonEmptyStr,
  firmware: BmcFirmwareReleaseIdentity,
  phase: ReadinessPhase,
  opened_at: EpochMs,
  previous: EpochMs?,
  looks: Int,
) -> ReadinessWait
{
  let got = megarac.Media.GetRemoteConfigurations(
    bmc_host: bmc_host,
    cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
    csrf_token: csrf_token,
    max_time: megarac_media_read_max_time_operand(),
  )
  match clock_unix_millis_read() {
    ClockUnixMillisRefused { detail: d } => ReadinessWaitClockUnreadable { detail: d }
    ClockUnixMillisObserved { millis: now } => {
      let look = ReadinessLook { observed_at: now, reading: attach_readiness(answered: got.success, body: got.body, image_name: image_name, firmware: firmware) }
      match readiness_verdict(opened_at: opened_at, budget: megarac_readiness_budget_ms(), previous: previous, look: look, phase: phase, looks: looks + 1) {
        ReadinessReady { look: l, looks: n } => ReadinessWaitReady { look: l, looks: n }
        ReadinessWindowClosed { last: l, deadline: d, looks: n } => ReadinessWaitClosed { last: l, deadline: d, looks: n }
        ReadinessRefusedVerdict { look: l, looks: n } => ReadinessWaitRefused { look: l, looks: n }
        ReadinessClockIncoherent { opened_at: o, previous: p, look: l, looks: n } => ReadinessWaitClockIncoherent { opened_at: o, previous: p, look: l, looks: n }
        ReadinessLookAgain => {
          let _paced = sleep_delay_seconds_second_carrier_projection(duration: megarac_readiness_interval)
          megarac_await_readiness(
            bmc_host: bmc_host,
            cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
            csrf_token: csrf_token,
            image_name: image_name,
            firmware: firmware,
            phase: phase,
            opened_at: opened_at,
            previous: Present { value: now },
            looks: looks + 1,
          )
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

fn megarac_readiness_outcome(
  bmc_host: NonEmptyStr,
  cookie_jar: NonEmptyStr,
  csrf_token: NonEmptyStr,
  image_name: NonEmptyStr,
  firmware: BmcFirmwareReleaseIdentity,
  route: MegaRacAttachRoute,
  phase: ReadinessPhase,
  cd_before: CdErrorReading,
) -> MegaRacAttachOutcome
{
  return match clock_unix_millis_read() {
    ClockUnixMillisRefused { detail: d } => MegaRacReadinessClockUnreadable { image_name: image_name, route: route, detail: d }
    ClockUnixMillisObserved { millis: opened_at } => {
      let wait = megarac_await_readiness(
        bmc_host: bmc_host,
        cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
        csrf_token: csrf_token,
        image_name: image_name,
        firmware: firmware,
        phase: phase,
        opened_at: opened_at,
        previous: none,
        looks: 0,
      )
      let general = megarac_raw_general(bmc_host: bmc_host, cookie_jar: cookie_jar, csrf_token: csrf_token)
      readiness_wait_outcome(
        wait: wait,
        image_name: image_name,
        firmware: firmware,
        route: route,
        cd_before: cd_before,
        general_at_end: general,
      )
    }
  }
}

// THE CODE IS READ AT THE END OF THE WAIT WHATEVER THE WAIT ANSWERED, so a refusal carries the code
// that stood beside the unhealthy presentation, and a ready presentation carries it beside the Started row, as an observation.
// PURE: the wait's answer as the attach outcome. Only a Started look reaches MegaRacPresentationReady,
// and the evidence is read from that look's row, so the record a boot is gated on is the row that
// satisfied the policy.
fn readiness_wait_outcome(
  wait: ReadinessWait,
  image_name: NonEmptyStr,
  firmware: BmcFirmwareReleaseIdentity,
  route: MegaRacAttachRoute,
  cd_before: CdErrorReading,
  general_at_end: MegaRacRawRead,
) -> MegaRacAttachOutcome {
  let cd_at_end = cd_error_of_raw(r: general_at_end, firmware: firmware)
  match wait {
    ReadinessWaitClockUnreadable { detail: d } => MegaRacReadinessClockUnreadable { image_name: image_name, route: route, detail: d }
    ReadinessWaitClockIncoherent { opened_at: o, previous: p, look: l, looks: n } => MegaRacReadinessClockIncoherent { image_name: image_name, route: route, opened_at: o, previous: p, look: l, looks: n }
    ReadinessWaitClosed { last: l, deadline: d, looks: n } =>
      MegaRacReadinessTimedOut { image_name: image_name, route: route, last: l, deadline: d, looks: n, cd_before_any_write: cd_before, cd_at_refusal: cd_at_end }
    ReadinessWaitRefused { look: l, looks: n } =>
      MegaRacReadinessRefused { image_name: image_name, route: route, look: l, looks: n, cd_before_any_write: cd_before, cd_at_refusal: cd_at_end }
    ReadinessWaitReady { look: l, looks: n } => {
      let not_ready = MegaRacReadinessRefused { image_name: image_name, route: route, look: l, looks: n, cd_before_any_write: cd_before, cd_at_refusal: cd_at_end }
      let state_unestablished = MegaRacMediaStateUnestablished { image_name: image_name, route: route, look: l, looks: n, cd_before_any_write: cd_before, cd_at_ready: cd_at_end, general_at_ready: general_at_end }
      match l.reading {
        ReadinessStarted { row: r } =>
          match cd_at_end {
            CdErrorUnread { detail: _ } => state_unestablished
            CdErrorRead { code: _ } =>
          MegaRacPresentationReady {
            route: route,
            evidence: MegaRacPresentationEvidence {
              firmware: firmware,
              image_name: image_name,
              media_index: r.media_index,
              session_index: r.session_index,
              redirection_wire: r.redirection_wire,
              established_at: l.observed_at,
              looks: n,
              cd_before_any_write: cd_before,
              cd_at_ready: cd_at_end,
              general_at_ready: general_at_end,
            },
          }
          }
        ReadinessConnecting { row: _ } => not_ready
        ReadinessStartedUnbound { row: _ } => not_ready
        ReadinessNotPresented { configurations: _ } => not_ready
        ReadinessUnanswered { detail: _ } => not_ready
        ReadinessUncatalogued { image_name: _, wire: _, configurations: _ } => not_ready
        ReadinessMalformed { detail: _ } => not_ready
        ReadinessDuplicate { configurations: _ } => not_ready
        ReadinessWrongPresentation { image_name: _, configurations: _ } => not_ready
      }
    }
  }
}

// ─── OBSERVING A PRESENTATION WITHOUT WRITING ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// One look at the three members that together say "this unit is being served this image": the share
// binding (with its CD error code) and the configurations row. Nothing is written. The readiness
// reading uses the already-presented phase: at this point the image was observed Started, so its
// absence is a withdrawal, not a pending start.
fn megarac_observe_with_token(
  bmc_host: NonEmptyStr,
  cookie_jar: NonEmptyStr,
  csrf_token: NonEmptyStr,
  image_name: NonEmptyStr,
  firmware: BmcFirmwareReleaseIdentity,
  share: MegaRacShareBinding,
) -> MegaRacAttachOutcome
{
  let general = megarac_raw_general(bmc_host: bmc_host, cookie_jar: cookie_jar, csrf_token: csrf_token)
  let c = megarac.Media.GetRemoteConfigurations(
    bmc_host: bmc_host,
    cookie_jar: cookie_jar,
    csrf_token: csrf_token,
    max_time: megarac_media_read_max_time_operand(),
  )
  let configurations = MegaRacRawRead { answered: c.success, body: c.body, observed_at: megarac_clock_at() }
  return MegaRacPresentationObserved {
    share: if general.answered { share_binding_standing(body: general.body, expected: share) } else { ShareUnreadable { detail: general.body } },
    readiness: attach_readiness(answered: configurations.answered, body: configurations.body, image_name: image_name, firmware: firmware),
    cd_error: cd_error_of_raw(r: general, firmware: firmware),
    general: general,
    configurations: configurations,
  }
}

// THREE ANSWERS, BECAUSE THEY ARE DIFFERENT FACTS (side-chat review 5331738657). Affirmed: the look
// was taken and the medium is not being served (a withdrawn or non-Started row, a share mismatch). Unobserved: the
// look itself failed (session, transport, an unread member, an unread cd_error_code), which says
// nothing about the medium. A read cd_error_code beside a Started row is recorded as an observation and
// does not withhold, because a Started row with a bound session is what the readiness policy asks for.
// And the look's own session must be released: a ready medium observed through a session the
// controller still holds is a cleanup obligation unmet, exactly as at the initial gate. Only
// PresentationStillReady admits a handoff; each other answer withholds and says which it was.
type PresentationStillServed
  = PresentationStillReady
  | PresentationReadyButSessionHeld { held: SessionRelease }
  | PresentationNoLongerReady { reason: NonEmptyStr }
  | PresentationUnobserved { reason: NonEmptyStr }

fn presentation_still_served(result: MegaRacAttachResult) -> PresentationStillServed {
  match result.outcome {
    MegaRacPresentationObserved { share: sh, readiness: r, cd_error: cd, general: _, configurations: _ } =>
      match sh {
        ShareUnreadable { detail: _ } => PresentationUnobserved { reason: "the general settings could not be read" }
        ShareMismatch { observed: _ } => PresentationNoLongerReady { reason: "the controller's share no longer matches this unit's boot share" }
        ShareBound => {
          let no_longer_ready = PresentationNoLongerReady { reason: "the configurations row is no longer Started with a bound session" }
          match r {
            ReadinessUnanswered { detail: _ } => PresentationUnobserved { reason: "the configurations read was not answered" }
            ReadinessMalformed { detail: _ } => PresentationUnobserved { reason: "the configurations document could not be read" }
            ReadinessUncatalogued { image_name: _, wire: _, configurations: _ } => PresentationUnobserved { reason: "a configurations row carries an uncatalogued status" }
            ReadinessStarted { row: _ } =>
              match cd {
                CdErrorUnread { detail: _ } => PresentationUnobserved { reason: "cd_error_code could not be read" }
                CdErrorRead { code: _ } =>
                  match result.session_release {
                    SessionReleased => PresentationStillReady
                    other => PresentationReadyButSessionHeld { held: other }
                  }
              }
            ReadinessConnecting { row: _ } => no_longer_ready
            ReadinessStartedUnbound { row: _ } => no_longer_ready
            ReadinessNotPresented { configurations: _ } =>
              no_longer_ready
            ReadinessDuplicate { configurations: _ } => no_longer_ready
            ReadinessWrongPresentation { image_name: _, configurations: _ } => no_longer_ready
          }
        }
      }
    MegaRacPresentationReady { route: _, evidence: _ } => presentation_unobserved_before_presentation()
    MegaRacReadinessTimedOut { image_name: _, route: _, last: _, deadline: _, looks: _, cd_before_any_write: _, cd_at_refusal: _ } => presentation_unobserved_before_presentation()
    MegaRacMediaStateUnestablished { image_name: _, route: _, look: _, looks: _, cd_before_any_write: _, cd_at_ready: _, general_at_ready: _ } => presentation_unobserved_before_presentation()
    MegaRacMediaStateUnestablishedBeforeWrite { cd_before_any_write: _, reason: _ } => presentation_unobserved_before_presentation()
    MegaRacReadinessRefused { image_name: _, route: _, look: _, looks: _, cd_before_any_write: _, cd_at_refusal: _ } => presentation_unobserved_before_presentation()
    MegaRacReadinessClockUnreadable { image_name: _, route: _, detail: _ } => presentation_unobserved_before_presentation()
    MegaRacReadinessClockIncoherent { image_name: _, route: _, opened_at: _, previous: _, look: _, looks: _ } => presentation_unobserved_before_presentation()
    MegaRacConfigurationsUnreadable { detail: _ } => presentation_unobserved_before_presentation()
    MegaRacShareMismatch { expected: _, observed: _ } => presentation_unobserved_before_presentation()
    MegaRacShareUnreadable { detail: _ } => presentation_unobserved_before_presentation()
    MegaRacSessionRefused { detail: _ } => presentation_unobserved_before_presentation()
    MegaRacSessionTokenUnreadable { detail: _ } => presentation_unobserved_before_presentation()
    MegaRacImagesUnreadable { detail: _ } => presentation_unobserved_before_presentation()
    MegaRacImageListingEmpty => presentation_unobserved_before_presentation()
    MegaRacImageListingUnparseable { detail: _ } => presentation_unobserved_before_presentation()
    MegaRacImageNotEnumerated { image_name: _ } => presentation_unobserved_before_presentation()
    MegaRacImageOfferedAmbiguously { image_name: _, image_indices: _ } => presentation_unobserved_before_presentation()
    MegaRacForeignImagePresented { image_name: _, configurations: _ } => presentation_unobserved_before_presentation()
    MegaRacSeveralImagesPresented { configurations: _ } => presentation_unobserved_before_presentation()
    MegaRacStaleDetachNotAdmitted { stale_image: _, reason: _ } => presentation_unobserved_before_presentation()
    MegaRacStaleDetachUnconfirmed { detach: _, reason: _ } => presentation_unobserved_before_presentation()
    MegaRacRedirectionUncatalogued { image_name: _, wire: _, configurations: _ } => presentation_unobserved_before_presentation()
    MegaRacRefreshClockUnreadable { detail: _, detach: _ } => presentation_unobserved_before_presentation()
    MegaRacListingUnparseableAfterDetach { detail: _, detach: _ } => presentation_unobserved_before_presentation()
    MegaRacOfferedAmbiguouslyAfterDetach { image_name: _, image_indices: _, detach: _ } => presentation_unobserved_before_presentation()
    MegaRacNotEnumeratedAfterRefresh { image_name: _, detach: _, standing: _ } => presentation_unobserved_before_presentation()
  }
}

fn presentation_unobserved_before_presentation() -> PresentationStillServed {
  PresentationUnobserved { reason: "the presentation could not be observed (the session was refused or its token unreadable)" }
}
